    "text_full": "Toggle navigation\nSearch\nDONATE\nHome\n \nExplanation\n \nAnswering Myths\n \nVideos\n \nEmail Your Legislator\n \nLetter-to-Editor\n \nVolunteer\n \nMedia\n \nAbout\n \nEvents\n\nState status: AK AL AR AZ CA CO CT DC DE FL GA HI IA ID IL IN KS KY LA MA MD ME MI MN MO MS MT NC ND NE NH NJ NM NV NY OH OK OR PA RI SC SD TN TX UT VA VT WA WI WV WY\n\nIndiana\nAsk your Indiana state legislators to pass the National Popular Vote bill\nSend a letter-to-the-editor to Indiana newspapers\nNational Popular Vote’s Facebook page\nNational Popular Vote’s Twitter page\n\nIn January 2019, State Senator Karen Tallian introduced the National Popular Vote bill in the Indiana Senate (status of SB212), as reported in NWI Times article.\n\nIn January 2017, Sen. Mark Stoops introduced the National Popular Vote bill (Status of SB372).\n\nOn February 3, 2007, Indiana state Representatives Matt Pierce and F. Dale Grubb introduced the National Popular Vote bill (HB 1807).\n\nThe national popular vote winner should become President\nOne-person, one-vote\nCandidates should have a reason to campaign in all 50 states"
}